		</div><div class="box"><a class="content-box"  href="/press/blog/date/2026/html/ecb.blog20260402~d9be74e490.en.html">
                    <div data-image="/press/blog/date/2026/html//ecb.blog20260402~d9be74e490/ecb.blog20260402~d9be74e490.jpg"></div>
                    <h5>2 April 2026</h5>
                    <h3>How banks are adjusting to declining reserves</h3>
                    <p>As the Eurosystem normalises its balance sheet, central bank reserves – banks’ most liquid asset – keep declining. This post examines how banks adapt to lower levels of reserves and explains why take-up in the Eurosystem’s standard refinancing operations is expected to increase.</p>
                </a>
				<div class="ecb-langSelector"><span class="offeredLanguage"><a  class='arrow' lang="en" href="/press/blog/date/2026/html/ecb.blog20260402~d9be74e490.en.html">
