		</div><div class="box"><a class="content-box"  href="/press/blog/date/2026/html/ecb.blog20260331~af8055c801.en.html">
                    <div data-image="/press/blog/date/2026/html//ecb.blog20260331~af8055c801/ecb.blog20260331~af8055c801.jpg"></div>
                    <h5>31 March 2026</h5>
                    <h3>From peak back to target: tracking expectations during the inflation surge</h3>
                    <p>Inflation expectations are crucial for monetary policy as they shape economic decisions and feed through to inflation. While expectation surveys provide insights, they come with blind spots. We use a model to transform infrequent survey data into a dense grid of expectations.</p>
                </a>
				<div class="ecb-langSelector"><span class="offeredLanguage"><a  class='arrow' lang="en" href="/press/blog/date/2026/html/ecb.blog20260331~af8055c801.en.html">
