                    <h5>10 February 2022</h5>
                    <h3>Bottlenecks and monetary policy</h3>
                    <p>Looking at inflation dynamics, the relative price dislocations associated with bottlenecks are intrinsically short-term, Chief Economist Philip R. Lane writes in The ECB Blog. An increase in the relative price for a scarce item will stimulate new supply, while cooling demand.</p>
                </a>
